Overlay patch 0033: skybox stereo markers (soh z_vr_box_draw.c).
Device finding (2026-07-17, and the sm64coopdx port's D-031 before it —
"disorienting clouds"): OoT's skybox is drawn CENTERED ON THE CAMERA, so the
per-eye camera shift cancels for it — the sky lands at ZERO disparity (on the
panel plane) while the terrain recedes behind: occlusion says "farthest",
stereo says "nearest". The fix is infinity disparity for skybox draws
(skew-only, no eye translation), which needs the interpreter to KNOW which
triangles are skybox. Same mechanism the sm64coopdx port proved: bracket the
skybox display-list emission with G_NOOP sentinel tags (types 0x5A begin /
0x5B end — types 7/8 are LUS's disp-stack tags); the interpreter's noop
handler (0031) flips a flag, cleared defensively at every Run start. The
extra two commands are __IOS__-gated; desktop skybox output is unchanged.

--- a/soh/src/code/z_vr_box_draw.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/z_vr_box_draw.c
@@ -19,6 +19,15 @@
 
     Gfx_SetupDL_40Opa(gfxCtx);
 
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    /* SOH_IOS (overlay 0033): stereo skybox BEGIN sentinel (see header). */
+    {
+        Gfx* sohTag = POLY_OPA_DISP++;
+        sohTag->words.w0 = (uintptr_t)((G_NOOP << 24) | (0x5A << 16));
+        sohTag->words.w1 = 0;
+    }
+#endif
+
     // gsSPShaderTest(POLY_OPA_DISP++);
 
     /*gSPSegment(POLY_OPA_DISP++, 0x7, skyboxCtx->staticSegments[0]);
@@ -94,6 +103,15 @@
     gDPPipeSync(POLY_OPA_DISP++);
     // gsSPShaderTest2(POLY_OPA_DISP++);
 
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    /* SOH_IOS (overlay 0033): stereo skybox END sentinel. */
+    {
+        Gfx* sohTag = POLY_OPA_DISP++;
+        sohTag->words.w0 = (uintptr_t)((G_NOOP << 24) | (0x5B << 16));
+        sohTag->words.w1 = 0;
+    }
+#endif
+
     FrameInterpolation_RecordCloseChild();
     CLOSE_DISPS(gfxCtx);
 }
